 "analysis": {
  "criteria": [
   "Experiment M4: the pre-registered analysis (frozen by checksum in the manifest before any training).",
   "Agents: model-based growth-optimal agents v4 (model_kelly4: a learned regime-switching world model, tracked while",
   "trading, with version 3's cost-aware decision), six seeds per market, judged on their FINAL checkpoint (200,000 bars of",
   "experience) on six fresh rounds of 20 test runs (120 runs).",
   "References (not agents), on the same test runs:",
   "S1X, S2X, S6X  true-model filter: version 4's decision with the market's TRUE regime model, inferring the current",
   "regime from prices like the agent (the best a trader who knows the rules can do); the ORACLE, which is",
   "told the true current regime at every bar, is reported as an upper bound only",
   "S1C            Experiment M3's true-parameter cost-aware reference;   S6  the exact growth-optimal constant size",
   "Ablation (not agents; one criterion and reported): each switching-market agent's own single-regime model (K = 1,",
   "version 4's static fallback), deciding on the same runs, to measure what tracking regimes is worth.",
   "S1X, S2X, S6X (markets that switch regime at unannounced times): a seed succeeds if",
   "A1  mean log growth per run > 0 with its 95% bootstrap interval (120 runs) above 0",
   "A2  growth above the matched-random 95th percentile in at least 5 of the 6 rounds",
   "A3  mean growth per run >= 50% of the true-model filter's mean growth on the same 120 runs",
   "A4  not more deaths than the true-model filter beyond chance: of the runs in which exactly one of the two died, the",
   "agent's share is not significantly above one half (exact one-sided binomial test, p >= 0.05). (No absolute",
   "ceiling: in design simulations the true-model filter itself died in 5 of 20 S2X runs; full growth-optimal",
   "sizing of a weak signal that can silently reverse is inherently risky, which the report states.)",
   "A5  adaptation is real: the agent's growth minus its own single-regime model's growth on the same runs is > 0 with a",
   "95% bootstrap interval (paired over the 120 runs) above 0",
   "E   decisions at 1,000x or more < 0.1%; rejected orders <= 0.1%; size output at the upper end of its range < 0.1%",
   "S1C (no change; regression check against version 3): Experiment M3's S1C criteria (m3_analysis.flags_predictable:",
   "C1-C5, E) against the M3 true-parameter reference.",
   "S6 (no change, no costs; regression check against version 2): Experiment M2's S6 criteria (m2_analysis.flags_s6:",
   "W1, W2', W3, W4, W5', W6, W7', E) against the exact optimum.",
   "A market passes if at least 4 of its 6 seeds succeed. M4 passes if all five markets pass.",
   "Reported, not criteria: oracle growth and deaths; regimes found (number, parameters, spell lengths); death rates."
  ],
  "file": "src/tradeworld/learning/m4_analysis.py"
 },
 "approval_conditions": [
  "2026-11-19: the owner gave full control of the project to pursue its aim (autonomous agents that discover profitable opportunities, size positions intelligently and learn from experience) without further approvals; on 2026-11-21 the owner said to start stage 6 (adapting when the market changes).",
  "Motivation (Experiment M3): version 3 profits after costs but learns once and keeps its model; markets change. Version 4 learns a regime-switching world model from its own experience (how many moods, how each behaves, how long each lasts) and tracks the current one while trading; with one regime it is a static model, so unchanging markets are checked too (S1C, S6). Design prototypes (seeds below 10,000) are documented in docs/experiments/m4_design.md.",
  "Kept: all earlier agents, versions, checkpoints, registries, evaluations, rewards and scoring rules untouched; earlier markets byte-identical (tested); nothing about the market given to the agents (the hidden regime path is used only by the labelled oracle reference); no exposure caps, penalties or trading style; criteria and code frozen by checksum before training; final checkpoints only; every seed reported."
 ],
 "compute": {
  "ablations": 18,
  "agents": 30,
  "estimate": "about 2-3 hours of training and 3-4 hours of evaluation on 4 cores",
  "references": 8
 },
 "data_points": [
  20000,
  200000
 ],
 "decision_quality": {
  "checksum": "0d0c6486487edacee4b54a34180d63855d77c413ab79e5bb15f27616aa292147",
  "definition": "Per decision with net exposure G (position value / equity): s(G) = max(g(G) / g(G*), F), and s(G) = F for a ruinous decision. g(G) = (1 - p) E_Z[ln(1 + G (e^(m + sigma Z) - 1))] + p ln(1 - G J) is the exact expected log growth of holding G for one decision (96-point Gauss-Hermite quadrature; minus infinity if G >= 1/J). G* = argmax g. F = g(G_ruin) / g(G*), the score of the smallest ruinous long position (G_ruin = 0.95 / J in S6; for a market without crashes, the size at which a 5-sigma fall reaches the 5% death line). Ruinous: G >= G_ruin long, or |G| >= 0.95 / (e^(m + 5 sigma) - 1) short. Q2 of an episode = mean of s over its decisions; Q2 of an evaluation = mean of the episode values. Uses only the decisions and the market's known parameters, never realised returns.",
  "frozen": true,
  "note": "used for S6 only",
  "version": "Q2.0"
 },
 "env_settings": {
  "decision_interval": 1,
  "obs_resolution": 1,
  "window": 30
 },
